 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S443-015\", \"clauses\": {\"read_and_write\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F18\", \"template\": \"Write the number: {word_form}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F18 has the learner read a number written in words and write its numeral. Its word_form slot is a repeats-a-generated-value domain printed as three-digit number words, and F18 is not in the failing families.\"}, \"numerals\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F19\", \"template\": \"Write {number} in words.\", \"reasoning\": \"F19 prints a numeral in question_text. Observed printed_runs run from 208 to 991, so the numerals object is shown to the learner.\"}, \"up_to_1000\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F19\", \"template\": \"Write {number} in words.\", \"reasoning\": \"F19 prints numerals across the three-digit range, observed 208 to 991, within declared_bounds 10 to 1000.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F08\", \"F10\", \"F11\", \"F12\", \"F15\", \"F16\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"{chunk}-{v}\", \"{p0}\", \"{p0} {p1}\", \"{v} hundred\", \"The number written as '{word}' is {fill_value}\", \"The number {number} is written in words as '{fill_value}'\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F08 chunk draws from the _TENS list, which includes the empty member, and v draws from _ONES, which includes the teen members. The template can therefore print a tens word followed by a teen word, or a dangling hyphen with an empty part, which is not a number word. F10 draws p0 from _ONES, which includes the empty member, so F10 can print a blank answer choice in distractors. F11 p0 is nested from F12 and F14. F14 members are full number words, and p1 can add an ones or tens word after them, which yields malformed text. F11 can also print a trailing space when p1 is empty. F12 draws v from _ONES, which includes the empty member, giving a leading space before hundred, and the teen members, giving a tens-of-hundreds value above 1000 that is outside the lc's range. F15 and F16 fill_value distractors include the number word for 884 (F15 fill_value lists 884, F15 word repeats word_form, and the printed word_form list includes the word for 884). A problem can therefore print a true statement in a distractor position, which is misleading. F16 has the same collision: number can be 884 and the distractor list includes the word for 884. F09, F13, F14 (as a standalone distractor), F17, F18 and F19 print only values that are valid for this lc within the observed domains.\"}",
